/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - The air load is spread over the whole control surface.
   - M is the hinge moment in N·m; q is the dynamic pressure in Pa; ρ is air density in kg/m³; V is true airspeed in m/s; S is the surface area in m²; c is its chord (mean width) in m; and Ch is the dimensionless hinge moment coefficient, set by
   - Two things make M grow fast.
   - A pilot can pull a few hundred newtons for a moment and much less for a long hold.
   - A power-assisted system — also called boosted, servo-assisted or partial power — keeps the mechanical link and adds a hydraulic actuator in parallel with it.
   - The follow-up linkage is position feedback.
   - If the hydraulics fail, the pilot can still fly.
   - A fully powered system — also called irreversible or all-powered — deletes the manual path.
   - Irreversible means the surface cannot drive back.
   - Power-actuated systems go further.
*/
