/* book exam traps: Saying a fully powered aircraft needs no feel system. It is the exact opposite: with the link gone, artificial feel is the only thing giving the pilot any stick force. | Calling a boosted system irreversible. A power-assisted system keeps the mechanical link and can revert to manual, with heavy forces. | Using V instead of V² in q, or dropping the chord c. Treat c and Ch as separate factors; Ch is dimensionless, c is in metres. | Thinking the follow-up linkage adds feel. It is position feedback that closes the loop and stops the surface at the commanded angle. | Believing higher hydraulic pressure gives a faster surface. Pressure sets the force; flow sets the rate. */
