/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - In an irreversible powered control the actuator carries the whole hinge moment.
   - q is dynamic pressure in Pa (N/m²); ρ is air density in kg/m³, about 1.225 at sea level in the standard atmosphere; V is true airspeed in m/s.
   - Hinge moment grows roughly with q times deflection.
   - The unit is called artificial or synthetic feel.
   - A tab is a small aerofoil hinged at the trailing edge of a main surface.
   - In a servo tab system the pilot's linkage drives only the tab; the main surface is free to float on its hinge.
   - The anti-servo tab is the mirror image: geared to move with the surface, it increases hinge moment and resists the pilot.
*/
